{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#lem:dc-ch5-2-1-parallel-frame","title":"lem:dc-ch5-2-1-parallel-frame","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields.md","line":24,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields.tex#lem:dc-ch5-2-1-parallel-frame","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#def:dc-ch2-2-5]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch5-2-1-parallel-frame","line":64,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[parallel orthonormal frame along a geodesic, coordinate form]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch5-2-1-parallel-frame}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch2-2-5, lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord}\n  \\dcref{ch5:2.1}\n  Along a geodesic $\\gamma:[0,a]\\to M$, every orthonormal basis of\n  $T_{\\gamma(0)}M$ extends uniquely to a parallel orthonormal frame\n  $e_1(t),\\dots,e_n(t)$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\sketch\n  Extend the initial basis by parallel transport. The inner products\n  $\\langle e_i,e_j\\rangle$ are constant by\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord}, hence remain equal to $\\delta_{ij}$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[parallel orthonormal frame along a geodesic, coordinate form] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368352d322d312d706172616c6c656c2d6672616d65\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23def%3Adc-ch2-2-5\">↗ def:dc-ch2-2-5</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23lem%3Adc-ch2-3-1-coord\">↗ lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch5:2.1</span></span>Along a geodesic <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :[0,a]\\to M$\">$\\gamma :[0,a]\\to M$</span>, every orthonormal basis of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_{\\gamma (0)}M$\">$T_{\\gamma (0)}M$</span> extends uniquely to a parallel orthonormal frame <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$e_1(t),\\dots ,e_n(t)$\">$e_1(t),\\dots ,e_n(t)$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Extend the initial basis by parallel transport. The inner products <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\langle e_i,e_j\\rangle $\">$\\langle e_i,e_j\\rangle $</span> are constant by <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23lem%3Adc-ch2-3-1-coord\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368322d332d312d636f6f7264\">section lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord</a>, hence remain equal to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\delta _{ij}$\">$\\delta _{ij}$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-2-1","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#lem:dc-ch5-2-1-ode","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#def:dc-ch2-2-5","title":"def:dc-ch2-2-5","label":"def:dc-ch2-2-5"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord","title":"lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord","label":"lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#def:dc-ch5-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch5-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch5-2-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#lem:dc-ch5-2-1-frame-reduction","title":"lem:dc-ch5-2-1-frame-reduction","label":"lem:dc-ch5-2-1-frame-reduction"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#lem:dc-ch5-2-1-frame-existence","title":"lem:dc-ch5-2-1-frame-existence","label":"lem:dc-ch5-2-1-frame-existence"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#lem:dc-ch5-2-7-frame-smooth","title":"lem:dc-ch5-2-7-frame-smooth","label":"lem:dc-ch5-2-7-frame-smooth"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#lem:dc-ch5-2-1-parallel-frame","title":"lem:dc-ch5-2-1-parallel-frame","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[parallel orthonormal frame along a geodesic, coordinate form]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch5-2-1-parallel-frame}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch2-2-5, lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord}\n  \\dcref{ch5:2.1}\n  Along a geodesic $\\gamma:[0,a]\\to M$, every orthonormal basis of\n  $T_{\\gamma(0)}M$ extends uniquely to a parallel orthonormal frame\n  $e_1(t),\\dots,e_n(t)$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\sketch\n  Extend the initial basis by parallel transport. The inner products\n  $\\langle e_i,e_j\\rangle$ are constant by\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord}, hence remain equal to $\\delta_{ij}$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#def:dc-ch2-2-5","title":"def:dc-ch2-2-5","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord","title":"lem:dc-ch2-3-1-coord","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}